  "scopeNotes": [
    "Availability lifecycle begins with explicit preexisting hub, queue, DA-parameter, correction-lock and DA bond pool genesis fixtures; all attestation and availability state is produced by evaluated ledger transactions, and Apply reads the pool as a Bonded reference input.",
    "Measured under the preprod-testing profile (720 s small and 840 s full response windows, one 20 s emulator block per transaction). The maximum-first-chunk scenario opens all 16 tranches with 19 outputs, publishes one maximum chunk of the first tranche and the second tranche's partial response, settles all 16 and times out with a full pool slash and queue removal.",
    "The complete-response scenario (301 chunks across two tranches) does not fit the testing windows and was skipped; it is measured only with a long-window profile (preprod-public or mainnet). The earlier 300-chunk maximum and complete-response measurements predate the pooled DA bond and are not carried forward.",
    "onchainRefusalCount counts the refusals the reported scenarios confirmed as Scalus CEK failures of the expected script and purpose; refusals in unreported scenarios are not counted.",
    "Roles lists the availability-challenge dispatcher and yields and the DA bond pool (one applied multivalidator published under its spending and minting roles), taken from the full node-runtime publication roster under an all-zero one-shot outref.",
    "Scenario deployment identities are rederived in each test with generated public actor identities. Rerun current-blueprint tests for release acceptance; this saved summary is not itself a release gate."
